===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|mi}}, {{m|enm|my}}, apocopated form of {{m|enm|min}}, {{m|enm|myn}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mīn||my, mine}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*mīn}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*mīnaz||my, mine|pos=pron.}} (possessive of {{m|gem-pro|*ek||I}}), from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*méynos||my; mine}}.

Cognate with {{cog|fy|myn||my}}, {{cog|af|my||my}}, {{cog|nl|mijn||my}}, {{cog|de|mein||my}}, {{cog|sv|min||my}}. More at {{l|en|me}}.

====Determiner====
{{head|en|determiner|cat2=possessive determiners}}

# First-person singular possessive determiner. See [[Appendix:Possessive#English]].
## Belonging to [[me]].
##: ''I can't find '''my''' book.''
## Associated with [[me]].
##: '''''My''' seat at the restaurant was uncomfortable.''
##: ''Don't you know '''my''' name?''
##: ''I recognised him because he had attended '''my''' school.''
## Related to me.
##: '''''My''' parents won't let me go out tonight.''
##* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|book=1|page=10|lines=165-166|passage=From what conſummate vertue I have choſe / This perfect Man, by merit call'd '''my''' Son,}}
## In the possession of me.
##: ''I have to take '''my''' books back to the library soon.''

